      "updated_at": "2026-03-19T10:22:15Z",
      "body": "One subtle problem I realized is that the C implementation of `decimal` and the pure python implementation diverge slightly: in the C version, `mapping` is stored in a `signaldict` while in the python version, they are stored in a normal `dict`. This divergence only became apparent when trying to write a test using the reproducer. Wondering if it would be worthwhile to make both of these implementations have the same behavior or if I should just change the C implementation (i.e. what I suggested above).  ",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
