      "body": "> Wondering if it would be worthwhile to make both of these implementations have the same behavior\n\nI don't think, that making behavior compatible is an easy task.  There are also a lot of other differences here, e.g.:\n```\n>>> import decimal\n>>> import _pydecimal\n>>> ctx_py = _pydecimal.Context(prec=7)\n>>> ctx_c = decimal.Context(prec=7)\n>>> del ctx_py.traps[_pydecimal.Clamped]\n>>> del ctx_c.traps[decimal.Clamped]\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<python-input-7>\", line 1, in <module>\n    del ctx_c.traps[decimal.Clamped]\n        ~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nValueError: signal keys cannot be deleted\n```\n\n> or if I should just change the C implementation (i.e. what I suggested above).\n\nYou also could check if traps/flags are uniquely referenced (and skip Py_CLEAR, if not).\n\nCC @serhiy-storchaka ",
