      "updated_at": "2026-03-22T22:46:52Z",
      "body": "The main issue I faced was with finding a way to write a test that covers both the C and Python implementations. As you explained, these implementations differ particularly using a `signaldict` vs a `dict`. I could write a test that covers just the C implementation; however, I feel like we should make both implementations as similar as possible. But this might end up being a big change and so I don't know where to go from here. \n\n> You also could check if traps/flags are uniquely referenced (and skip Py_CLEAR, if not).\n\nGood idea!",
